12a. Calls on the Commission to introduce targeted regulatory simplification and increased flexibility for Member States in the implementation of EU legislation that has a direct or indirect negative impact on housing supply and affordability, such as the Energy Performance of Buildings Directive1a, the Energy Efficiency Directive1b, the Ambient Air Quality Directive1c, and the Habitats Directive1d, among other relevant EU legislation; stresses that, in the context of the ongoing housing crisis across the EU, Member States must be granted flexibility in spatial planning, adjust rigid principles such as the ‘one out, all out’ rule and strict non-deterioration requirements, reduce excessive monitoring and reporting obligations, ensure proportionate environmental and energy standards, and allow targeted exemptions for housing-related projects;

---

1a Directive (EU) 2024/1275 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 24 April 2024 on the energy performance of buildings (OJ L, 2024/1275, 8.5.2024, ELI:[http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/1275/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/1275/oj)). 1b Directive (EU) 2023/1791 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 13 September 2023 on energy efficiency and amending Regulation (EU) 2023/955 (OJ L 231, 20.9.2023, p. 1, ELI: [http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2023/1791/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2023/1791/oj)). 1c Directive (EU) 2024/2881 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 23 October 2024 on ambient air quality and cleaner air for Europe (OJ L, 2024/2881, 20.11.2024, ELI:[http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/2881/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/2881/oj)). 1d Council Directive 92/43/EEC of 21 May 1992 on the conservation of natural habitats and of wild fauna and flora (OJ L 206, 22.7.1992, p. 7, ELI: [http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/1992/43/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/1992/43/oj)).
